{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And let us know</b> — that we pursue knowing HaShem, for this is the secret of all wisdoms, and for this alone was man created; only, one cannot know HaShem until one learns many wisdoms, which are like a ladder to ascend to this supreme degree." "<b>As the dawn</b> — for at first the discerning one knows HaShem through His deeds like the dawn at its going forth, and moment by moment the light grows, until he sees the truth." "<b>And He shall come as rain</b> — the meaning is that HaShem will awaken us and teach us the truth, after the manner of (Deuteronomy 32:2) יערף כמטר לקחי ('My teaching shall drop as the rain'). And others said: for healing will come to us from HaShem, like rain that no man hopes for. And the meaning is: for there is no healing except from Him." "<b>As the latter rain, watering the earth</b> — it lacks a vav, in the manner of אדם שת ('the man, Seth') — also a bet may be elided, in the manner of כי ששת ימים ('for six days'). And thus it is כמלקוש ויורה ארץ ('like the latter rain watering the earth')."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:23.336546449Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}